 "description": "A full grid on her 3-block CNN, for Dr. Luitel's request of 2026-10-12 to compare grid, random and Bayesian search and to run every combination of a list of values per setting. Seven settings, each at her 3-block CNN's value and the tuned 3-block CNN's (threeblock_final): pooling mean or SD; 60 epochs with patience 10 or 100 with patience 20; channels 32-64-128 or 64-128-256; kernel 3 or 5; dropout 0.3 or 0.2; 64 or 40 mel bands; no hidden layer or 128 units. They are the seven with the largest spread of mean validation UA in cnn_3block_screen_1's random stage. Every other setting is cnn_3block_screen_1's base (her 3-block CNN as specified, training accuracy every epoch). 128 configurations, seeds 1 to 3, session-out folds, four classes: 1,920 jobs. Validation only: the comparison of search methods is fixed in PLAN_night13.txt (analyses/night13_prep_20261012) before any run, and no test file is read.",
